      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:50:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like C Binder has the same partial-page issue. In a 4KB process the VMA can end partway through a native page (libbinder maps 1MB - 2 * 4KB), but `pages[]` is sized `buffer_size / PAGE_SIZE` here, and the loops at lines 1014 and 1091 use the same bound.\n\nSo I think a buffer in the last partial page would index past the array, and that page would never be freed. Would `DIV_ROUND_UP(alloc-\u003ebuffer_size, PAGE_SIZE)` in all three places work?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "875e42a99873a88a70dca9ec37d7856bed9c2067",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
