      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:50:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think `vm_insert_page()` already covers this: since aosp/4368056 it maps every slice of the page that lies in a 4KB VMA, clamped to `vm_end` (`vma_insert_page_slices()` in `mm/p3s/pgtable.h`), and Rust\u0027s `vm_insert_page()` calls straight into it.\n\nSince `vm_insert_page_native()` does the same, could Binder keep calling `vm_insert_page()`, and `vm_insert_page_native()` be dropped from `mm/memory.c`, `mm.h`, `binder_alloc.c` and `virt.rs`?\n\nThe size rounding and the zap clamp in `page_range.rs` look needed to me, since Rust\u0027s `zap_page_range_single()` silently returns when the range passes `vm_end`.",
